# Northgate AI Stock Predictor — repository contents
#
# The rule applied here: commit the CODE and the EVIDENCE, regenerate the DATA.
#
#   code    src/, dashboard/, tests/, scripts/, config.yaml, entry points
#   evidence reports/ — the written report, the data-quality report, the
#            mathematics verification, the EDA findings and figures. These are
#            the deliverables and the record of what was measured, so they are
#            versioned.
#   data    data/ and models/ are byte-identical outputs of
#            `python rebuild_dataset.py` and `python retrain_models.py`. They are
#            reproducible in about 40 minutes on a laptop, which is what PRD
#            Section 15.3 asks to be able to demonstrate, and the largest of them
#            is a single 18.6 MB parquet. Versioning them would put a
#            regenerable binary in the history forever.
#
# The small text artifacts the dashboard reads ARE committed, so the panels can
# be reviewed without a 40-minute rebuild:
#   data/processed/*_metrics.csv, model_leaderboard.csv, portfolio_metrics.json,
#   declared_model.json, cross_sectional_results.json, recommendations.csv

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Test and tooling caches ------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Data caches ------------------------------------------------------------
.yfinance-cache/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The Finnhub key is read from the environment variable named by
# `sentiment.api_key_env` in config.yaml. Nothing secret is ever committed; these
# lines exist so a local `.env` cannot be added by accident.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# --- Regenerable binary data (see the rule at the top) ----------------------
data/raw/
data/processed/*.parquet
data/processed/*.npy
data/processed/*.pkl
models/*.keras
models/*.pkl
models/*.joblib

# Not ignored, deliberately:
#   data/processed/*.csv, *.json   small metrics and results, committed as evidence
#   reports/**                     the written report and its figures
#   notebooks/eda.ipynb            runnable, and free of absolute paths

# --- OS noise ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
